  "native_adaptations": [
    "Typed TablePadding replaces integer pad flags. Crossing points use a fixed 12-entry array.",
    "Owned JSON scalar conversions and explicit Display adapter preserve text without PHP runtime object identity.",
    "Native Result propagates typed configuration, formatting and invalid UTF-8 padding errors; invalid bytes cannot be returned as a Rust String.",
    "The public symfony-style-guide preset name is retained as a compatibility identifier.",
    "PHP engine diagnostics such as NAN-to-string warnings are retained in reference evidence; the native typed scalar conversion returns NAN without emulating VM warnings.",
    "Keep existing read-only style getters and add _mut variants for safe mutable borrowing; no return-type break or dynamic mutable alias.",
    "Column indices remain native usize like existing column-style methods; signed i64 widths retain zero/negative rendering behavior. Sequential and indexed bulk variants express source array shapes without changing CLI/data formats.",
    "Propagate typed ConsoleTableError for unsupported wrapping or invalid effective widths, preserving source failure stage and already emitted output. Header Option<&str> clearing maps source nullable strings.",
    "PreparedLayout is private derived data, not another renderer. Source Table only expands a formatter result containing LF; otherwise original text, including raw newlines, is retained. Actual custom interface calls and output compared to source.",
    "Reuse support::ArrayKey canonical integer/string keys; preserve insertion position, negative-index next-key and checked i64 exhaustion. add_row now returns Result and add_rows propagates partial success; the existing in-repo caller is migrated to unwrap/?, CLI/data names unchanged.",
    "set_headers_rows is the native multiple-header counterpart of overloaded source array shape. Boolean direction setters explicitly restore Default when false; layout never destroys stored input rows.",
    "Vertical record separators are private derived cell markers with actual column style and wrapping behavior. They do not claim public TableSeparator/merged-cell options have been implemented."
  ],
  "remaining_sdk": [
    "Named mutable style definitions and shared reference lifecycle",
    "appendRow with actual ConsoleSectionOutput",
    "Explicit TableSeparator inputs, colspan/rowspan and per-cell style",
    "OutputStyle inherited table/create_table layout/counters and other component SDK remain separately reviewed in io-contracts"
  ]
